## 4. What this does and does not say about his 29

  His 29 is a CEILING on the behavioural blast radius under a key that is part census-derived
  and part scope-label. 5 of the 29 are claimed by the `**tools:**` scope label alone and by
  nothing else,
  and every tool-runner identifier they name occurs 0× in Klatch non-test source.
  Dropping that leg takes 29 -> 24. Both numbers are real: 29 is the figure under his
  published key, 24 is the figure under the census his own docblock says the key is derived
  from. Neither is a floor — UNMODELLED 90 remains the floor on the key's blindness.

  Not claimed here: that the lost rows cannot affect Klatch. "Klatch does not name the SDK
  tool-runner" is a source fact; whether a change to it can reach Klatch through a shared code
  path inside the SDK is NOT reachable from a source read, and is left UNMEASURED rather than
  asserted either way.

